<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Poljica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Poljica is a hilly district in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetina">Cetina</a> river, the Mosor mountains and the Adriatic coast south-east of Split. From the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> its villages governed themselves as an autonomous community under an elected grand knez, recognising in turn Croatian-Hungarian, Venetian and Ottoman overlords. Its autonomy, recorded in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poljica-statute">Poljica Statute</a>, lasted until the French abolished it in 1807.</p></div>
